      <groundspeak:encoded_hints>FGL 11.7M W. OF C/L OF N-S RD.

ASC BRASS CAP FLUSH WITH GRD.
55M S OF C/L OF E-W GRAVEL RD; 11.7M W OF C/L OF N-S GRAVEL RD; GP 3.283M E.</groundspeak:encoded_hints>
      <groundspeak:logs>
        <groundspeak:log id="496325242">
          <groundspeak:date>2015-04-25T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="664594">Sears Tower</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP232 - Lunnford&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This was an eventful cap.  First was that I put the coordinates n the vehicle GPSr incorrectly and was several kilometers away.  Then as I am on my way to correct my error, I was going through Dapp when I see a HUGE cloud of black smoke.  Apparently I farmers fuel take caught fire.  Fortunately, no one was hurt.  Finally, after over 30 minutes for wrong coordinates/fire watching, I made it to the cap.  TFTH&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="622372968">
          <groundspeak:date>2014-08-12T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="2395896">MKFmly</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP232 Lunnford &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Posted Coordinates: N54° 03.871 W114° 18.035

My GPSr Coordinates: N54° 03.871 W114° 18.035&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With a few days booked off we headed out on a caching and capping trip with a few objectives. Those objectives included having some fun and grabbing a few caches for various goals and challenges we have set for ourselves.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Wow it's been a long while since we found this cap. Just trying to get caught up again. It's always a pleasure to roam Alberta in search of the Brass.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;TFT Cap, outforthehunt!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="255729688">
          <groundspeak:log_wpt lat="54.064517" lon="-114.300583" />
          <groundspeak:date>2012-08-07T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="277147">rubiconrunner</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP232 Lunnford&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Came at it from the road side but then had to hop a barbed wire fence. If you approach from the north on the field side you just need to go underneath a single strand of barbed wire. TFTBC!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
